<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Month-grid widget provider info for API 26-30 (ROADMAP M5 T3; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Widget
  architecture", "Configuration"). API 31 and later reads res/xml-v31/month_widget_info.xml instead,
  which adds maxResizeWidth/Height, targetCellWidth/Height and previewLayout, all introduced in API 31,
  so lint's UnusedAttribute check (correctly) rejects them here at minSdk 26. A `-v31` resource file
  replaces this one entirely rather than merging with it, so keep both files in step.

  minWidth/minResizeWidth (ROADMAP M8 T1, accessibility audit finding #14): raised from 250dp to 320dp
  — not all the way to the 48dp touch-target floor (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §4 "Accessibility"), because
  that trade-off is real and stated honestly rather than hidden behind a rounder number. The arithmetic,
  from MonthGlanceWidget's own layout constants: MonthWidgetContent's outer Column pads the whole widget
  by 8dp on every side (16dp off the total width), and the seven columns then split what is left evenly
  (DayNumberCell's `defaultWeight()`), so one column's width is `(minWidth - 16dp) / 7`. Solving
  `(minWidth - 16) / 7 >= 48` gives `minWidth >= 352dp` — but a 352dp+ minimum does not fit a 360dp-wide
  phone's launcher grid (a 4-column grid there gives about `4 * 90 - 30 = 330dp`; a 5-column grid about
  `5 * 72 - 30 = 330dp`; both under 352dp), and a launcher that cannot fit a widget's declared minWidth
  refuses to place it at all, which is a worse outcome than a too-small cell. 320dp — five of the
  platform's nominal 70dp home-screen cells minus the 30dp gap it always subtracts (`70 * 5 - 30 = 320`)
  — is chosen instead because it fits that 360dp phone (330dp >= 320dp) while getting as close to the
  floor as that constraint allows: `(320 - 16) / 7 ~= 43.4dp` per column, about 5dp under the 48dp floor
  at this minimum. The floor is only actually met once a placement spans six or more of the launcher's
  nominal cells (about 390dp and up by the same `70 * cells - 30` formula); this file's real guarantee is
  "48dp met at any six-cell-or-larger placement, within 5dp of it at the five-cell minimum" — not "48dp
  everywhere", because a widget that cannot be placed helps no one. maxResizeWidth stays 460dp (seven
  cells, `70 * 7 - 30 = 460`) — already a valid, generous upper bound above the new minResizeWidth.
  targetCellWidth moves from 4 to 5 to match. Height is untouched: the finding was about the seven
  *columns*, and 180dp minHeight already gives every row well over 48dp (four rows, no shared horizontal
  division).

  Sizes otherwise match MonthGlanceWidget's SizeMode.Responsive steps in Kotlin (COMPACT/FULL):
  docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5's "Month grid: 4x3 and larger" describes the COMPACT/FULL breakpoints
  themselves, which are unchanged — SizeMode.Responsive selects between them by the widget's actual
  size at render time, not by this file's min/max attributes, so raising the resize floor here does not
  stop the widget from ever being small in Glance's eyes; a real device is simply never offered a
  narrower size to resize down to.

  updatePeriodMillis is the layer-3 self-healing backstop of the midnight rollover
  (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Midnight rollover (layered)"), the same four hours as the Today widget;
  layers 1 and 2 (the alarm and the system-event receivers in :core:scheduling) do the real work.

  widgetCategory is "home_screen" only (ROADMAP M5 T6 added event dots, which does not change this):
  docs/security-and-privacy.md §3.2's ruling is "any widget capable of showing event titles declares
  `not_keyguard`": a dot reveals only that a day has *something* on it (a plain boolean,
  `ObserveAgendaUseCase.presence`; CLAUDE.md rule 8), never a title, a count, or which calendar, so this
  widget is not "capable of showing event titles" in the sense that ruling means, and stays lock-screen
  eligible on Android 16 QPR2+ like the date-only Today widget, without declaring `not_keyguard`.

  previewImage (ROADMAP M5 T5) is valid since API 11 (confirmed against the SDK's own api-versions.xml,
  not from memory), so it belongs here rather than needing its own `-v30`/`-v31` split; it is the
  widget-picker preview shown below API 31, superseded by previewLayout at API 31-34 and by
  `providePreview`/`setWidgetPreview` at API 35+ (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5 "Picker previews").

  No android:configure: the optional config activity is ROADMAP M5 T4, out of scope here.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="320dp"
    android:minHeight="180dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="320dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="180dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="14400000"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/month_widget_loading"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview_image"
    android:description="@string/month_widget_description" />
